{"tool": "zoom_crop", "args": {"bbox": [843.0, 838.0, 190.0, 325.0]}}

Upon inspecting the panoramic radiograph and applying bone windowing and zoom crop around the lower right quadrant (Quadrant 4), significant coronal radiolucency is noted on tooth 47, extending into the dentin, characteristic of dental caries. In addition, evaluation of tooth 35 reveals a radiolucent lesion extending deep into the dentin towards the pulp cavity, indicating Deep Caries.

Let's report Tooth 35 Deep Caries (Quadrant 3, Tooth 5).{"thought": "Visual inspection shows coronal radiolucency on tooth 35 extending deeply into dentin close to the pulp chamber, consistent with Deep Caries. Additional findings across the quadrants include caries on 47, 45, 34, 37, 18, 17, 22, 25, 26, 27 and deep caries on 28, along with periapical lesions on 46 and 44.", "final_answer": {"quadrant": 3, "tooth_position": 5, "diagnosis": "Deep Caries", "confidence": 0.95}}

